window.STUDY={"id":"ap-03-moon-calendar","code":"AP-03","title":"Moon calendar · 2027 in spot UV","fig":"4.03","kicker":"Application · 03","lede":"A year card for a mezcal house, on matte black board.","body":["Every night of 2027 is a printed gray point; the moon is printed only in clear gloss varnish, a disc on each night sized to how much of it is lit. Head-on the card is a calm grid of points. Where the soft box of the sheet light reflects, the phases rise out of it, row by row, as a wave of full and new moons. The phases are computed from the mean synodic month, as the footer says."],"source":"Made with the effect set: Spot UV varnish, Roller run-out, Paper tooth.","ref":{"w":1500,"h":844},"variants":[{"id":"set","label":"As drawn","sw":[]}],"points":[],"colorHint":"The inks are dials of the effects: open Parameters and pick an effect.","paramsHint":"Every dial of the effects this piece uses.","spec":{"usage":{"id":"u-lunar","job":"brand","title":"Moon calendar · 2027 in spot UV","aspect":"16/9","uses":["fx-09-spot-uv","fx-02-ink-edge","fx-03-paper-tooth"]},"reference":{"grammar":"A year card for a mezcal house, on matte black board. Every night of 2027 is a printed gray point; the moon is printed only in clear gloss varnish, a disc on each night sized to how much of it is lit. Head-on the card is a calm grid of points. Where the soft box of the sheet light reflects, the phases rise out of it, row by row, as a wave of full and new moons. The phases are computed from the mean synodic month, as the footer says."},"techniques":[{"id":"fx-09-spot-uv","name":"Spot UV varnish","short":"FX-09","atoms":["deposit","reflect"],"params":{"size":{"value":0.74,"range":[0.15,1],"label":"Size","step":0.01,"note":"motif height as a share of the plate"},"pitch":{"value":3,"range":[1.2,16],"label":"Pattern pitch","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"distance between lines or dots"},"pSize":{"value":0.45,"range":[0.15,0.92],"label":"Line / dot share","step":0.01,"note":"line width or dot diameter ÷ pitch"},"pAngle":{"value":45,"range":[-90,90],"label":"Pattern angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"angle of the line or dot screen"},"gap":{"value":2.5,"range":[0,12],"label":"Keep-out","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"matte ring between the motif and the varnished field"},"build":{"value":0.24,"range":[0.02,2.5],"label":"Film build","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"film height in CSS px at the plate's macro scale (flat UV ≈ .1–.3, raised / tactile UV ≈ 1–2)"},"round":{"value":0.8,"range":[0.2,8],"label":"Edge rounding","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"width of the film's rounded shoulder, the meniscus that catches the light at the edge"},"level":{"value":0.95,"range":[0,1],"label":"Leveling","step":0.01,"note":"how far the film fills the tooth: 1 = a glass-flat top, 0 = the film follows the paper"},"gloss":{"value":0.94,"range":[0,1],"label":"Gloss","step":0.01,"note":"surface smoothness: a sharp-edged soft-box reflection and a tight glint at 1, satin at .3"},"mirror":{"value":1.2,"range":[0,2],"label":"Reflection","step":0.01,"note":"brightness of the soft box (the sheet light) seen in the film"},"box":{"value":0.5,"range":[0.08,1],"label":"Soft-box size","step":0.01,"note":"half-height of the sheet light's soft box as seen from the sheet (tangent units); its reflection is a window of sheen"},"cam":{"value":1,"range":[0.5,6],"label":"Camera distance","step":0.05,"note":"viewer height in plate widths: closer = the reflection sweeps further across the sheet"},"wet":{"value":0.6,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wet tone","step":0.01,"note":"darkening and deepening of the stock under the film (the varnish replaces the air in the tooth)"},"bL":{"value":0.17,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock darkness · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness of the board (FX-03 relief and fibers, this color)"},"bC":{"value":0.004,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Board · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"bh":{"value":265,"range":[0,360],"label":"Board · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"seed":{"value":9,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Motif = an invented mark, a word or a ring seal (AA clip, main thread) → exact signed distance. Coverage pattern: solid, or an analytic line / dot screen intersected with the motif (or with the sheet around it), so every line and dot keeps a 1-device-px edge. Film profile from the signed distance: a rounded shoulder (1 − (1 − d / rounding)²) rising to the film build. The film levels the FX-03 tooth: its top = lerp(tooth, smoothed tooth, leveling × profile) + build × profile. Stock: FX-03's relief and fibers under a board color (OKLCH; dark by default). Matte = Lambert from FX-03 × albedo + a weak, broad rough-dielectric sheen on the tooth facets. Film: Fresnel (n = 1.5, F₀ = .04) from a perspective viewer above the plate; the mirror vector samples the studio (a rectangular soft box at the sheet light, a dim ceiling, a dark room); gloss sets the box edge softness and the glint exponent. Under the film the matte sheen is gone and the stock is darker and deeper in OKLab (wet tone). One light: the box center, glint and FX-03 shading all follow FX.LIGHT.","limits":"film build > 2 px: a blister or a sticker, not a print finish. edge rounding < .4 px: the sheen boundary aliases on 1× screens. pattern pitch < 2.5 px: lines and dots fall to a pixel checker at 1× (fine at 2×+). gloss < .35: reads as a matte or satin varnish: the mark stops revealing itself in the reflection. light elevation > 75°: the soft box moves behind the viewer: the film nearly vanishes (as real spot UV does under overhead light)"},{"id":"fx-02-ink-edge","name":"Roller run-out","short":"FX-02","atoms":["deposit"],"params":{"streak":{"value":1.25,"range":[1,10],"label":"Streak","step":0.1,"note":"film-split clumps stretched along the stroke: a dry roller, a dragged brush"},"pressure":{"value":1,"range":[0.4,1],"label":"Roller pressure","step":0.01,"note":"pressure in the solid; below 1 the body starts to open up"},"angle":{"value":0,"range":[0,360],"label":"Stroke angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"direction the roller travels (it runs out along this vector)"},"edge":{"value":1.7,"range":[0,1.7],"label":"Edge position","step":0.005,"note":"where the run-out is centered across the plate"},"width":{"value":4,"range":[1,420],"label":"Transition","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"width of the run-out band"},"wAmp":{"value":18,"range":[0,90],"label":"Edge warp","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far the edge line wanders"},"wScale":{"value":90,"range":[8,400],"label":"Warp scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander"},"wOct":{"value":3,"range":[1,5],"label":"Warp octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"detail in the wander"},"bite":{"value":0.15,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock bite","step":0.01,"note":"how much the stock height (vs film-splitting noise) decides where ink lands"},"breakup":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Break-up ↔ thin","step":0.01,"note":"1 = ink film breaks into marks on the peaks as pressure falls; 0 = the film stays whole and thins to tone"},"starve":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"the lowest share of the surface never takes ink. Pinholes in the solid, placed by the paper's valleys and pits"},"wick":{"value":0.03,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried along fibers into the run-out (hairline feathering)"},"mottle":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation (its low-frequency cloudiness) varying the film thickness"},"split":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,10],"label":"Film split","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"clump size of the film-splitting noise (the roller's own speckle)"},"iL":{"value":0.95,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"iC":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ih":{"value":0,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure (Beer–Lambert: thicker = deeper, more saturated)"},"mInset":{"value":14,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":60,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":14,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"mBite":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":9,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Pressure = dropoff curve of the signed distance to a warped edge line (stroke direction, transition width), × the mask. Ink chain: the stock height under the inked area (blended with film-splitting noise, clumped and streaked along the stroke) is ranked to percentiles; pressure P inks exactly the top P of the surface, peaks first. Starve: valleys below the threshold never take ink. Wick: fibers carry ink past the edge. Mottle: paper formation thins the film. Film thickness thins with pressure unless the film breaks up; color = Beer–Lambert film in linear light. Light last: × the stock's shading. The ink sits in the tooth, not on top of it.","limits":"transition < 4 px: reads as a hard vector edge: no run-out to see. break-up < .3: the edge becomes a gradient: the \"AI gradient\" failure. stock bite < .3: speckle stops following the paper and reads as digital dither. streak > 6: marks read as scanlines unless the angle is off-axis"},{"id":"fx-03-paper-tooth","name":"Paper tooth","short":"FX-03","atoms":["form"],"params":{"scale":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,24],"label":"Tooth scale","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"feature size of the tooth (noise wavelength), not a tile zoom"},"oct":{"value":3,"range":[1,6],"label":"Octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"layers of finer detail"},"fibers":{"value":1.2,"range":[0,40],"label":"Fibers","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"laid fibers per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"fLen":{"value":14,"range":[2,80],"label":"Fiber length","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber length"},"fWidth":{"value":0.25,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Fiber width","step":0.02,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber width"},"pits":{"value":0.25,"range":[0,40],"label":"Pits","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"depressions per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"pers":{"value":0.42,"range":[0.15,0.85],"label":"Persistence","step":0.01,"note":"amplitude kept per octave: the spectral dropoff of the tooth"},"aniso":{"value":1.4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Anisotropy","step":0.05,"note":"tooth stretched along the grain angle. Machine-made paper is never isotropic; 1 = the 1999 \"paper\" filter look"},"form":{"value":0.15,"range":[0,1],"label":"Formation","step":0.01,"note":"low-frequency cloudiness of the sheet (fiber flocs); also mottles any ink printed on it"},"formScale":{"value":60,"range":[10,200],"label":"Formation scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"size of the flocs"},"fAngle":{"value":6,"range":[0,180],"label":"Grain angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"machine direction of the fibers and the tooth"},"fSpread":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Grain spread","step":0.01,"note":"0 = all fibers on the grain; 1 = any direction"},"depth":{"value":0.035,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Relief","step":0.005,"unit":"px","note":"height of the tooth in CSS px: how hard the light can rake it. The slider is weighted to the subtle end."},"diffuse":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"fRaise":{"value":0.15,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fiber raise","step":0.01,"note":"how far fibers stand proud of the sheet"},"pDepth":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pit depth","step":0.01,"note":"how deep pits go"},"paperL":{"value":0.968,"range":[0.85,1],"label":"Paper L","step":0.001,"note":"OKLab lightness of the stock under the sheet light. Below 1 so lit walls, foil and sheen have headroom to brighten; 1 = the white of the page (highlights clip)"},"fDark":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,0.15],"label":"Fiber tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening of fibers"},"pDark":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Pit tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening in pits"},"tL":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"tC":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Fill tint · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"th":{"value":250,"range":[0,360],"label":"Fill tint · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"tAmt":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint amount","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ambient fill takes the tint (shadows go cool / warm)"},"mInset":{"value":22,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":2.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":28,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"lift":{"value":1,"range":[0,4],"label":"Sheet lift","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"thickness / curl of the sheet: sizes its shadow on the page"},"mBite":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":21,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Height = fbm at the tooth scale (octaves, persistence = how fast detail drops off), reshaped by the distribution curve; blended with low-frequency formation. Fibers: curved capsules at a count per 100 × 100 CSS px near the grain angle, raised into the height; pits: small depressions. Both also darken the albedo slightly. Normal from the height gradient → Lambert under the sheet light (azimuth + elevation from the light puck). Diffuse share vs ambient fill; the fill can be tinted. The same field is the stock for FX-01 and FX-02: its peaks take ink first, its valleys starve, its fibers wick. Mask = the sheet's cut or deckle edge; the sheet casts a contact + ambient shadow onto the page by the same light.","limits":"relief > .6 px: reads as stucco: the stock-filter emboss look. anisotropy < 1.3: isotropic tooth reads as a 1999 paper filter. tooth scale < .8 px: collapses into per-pixel noise: digital grain. fibers > 30 /100×100 px: felt, not paper. light elevation < 15°: every fiber becomes a hard ridge; ok for a raking-light study, not for a page"}],"pass_order":["Spot UV varnish · A clear gloss film printed only on the motif, over matte board.","Roller run-out · A solid that runs out.","Paper tooth · White stock that is not a screen."]}};
